"working condition.The instructions say that it allows you to improve any "
"missile gun installed on the ship, so that it will not need ammunition!It "
"looks very attractive."

#: src-ru/data/events.xml.rawclobber:12091
msgid ""
"data/events.xml.rawclobber$//eventList[@name=\"PLANET_ENGE_BUNKER\"]/event[3]/choice[3]/text"
msgstr "Explore 10 missiles."

#: src-ru/data/events.xml.rawclobber:12096
msgid ""
"data/events.xml.rawclobber$//eventList[@name=\"PLANET_ENGE_BUNKER\"]/event[3]/choice[3]/event/text"
msgstr ""
"You lay a powerful charge of ten warheads under one of the doors.A deafening"
" explosion is heard, and part of the corridor near the door collapses!One of"
" your team is buried alive.It seems that you have overdid it with the power "
"of the charge ..."

#: src-ru/data/events.xml.rawclobber:12100
msgid ""
"data/events.xml.rawclobber$//eventList[@name=\"PLANET_ENGE_BUNKER\"]/event[3]/choice[3]/event/choice[@req=\"CREW_ALL\""
" and not(@lvl)]/event/text"
msgstr "Your crew member will not be enough."

#: src-ru/data/events.xml.rawclobber:12103
msgid ""
"data/events.xml.rawclobber$//eventList[@name=\"PLANET_ENGE_BUNKER\"]/event[3]/choice[3]/event/choice[@req=\"CREW_ALL\""
" and not(@lvl)]/event/removeCrew/text"
msgstr "The clone of the deceased appears in a clone-haze."

#: src-ru/data/events.xml.rawclobber:12110
msgid ""
"data/events.xml.rawclobber$//eventList[@name=\"PLANET_ENGE_BUNKER\"]/event[3]/choice[3]/event/choice[@req=\"CREW_ALL\""
" and @lvl=\"0\"]/event/text"
msgstr ""
"Since your ship is controlled by AI, you should not be afraid of the death "
"of the entire crew."

#: src-ru/data/events.xml.rawclobber:12116
msgid ""
"data/events.xml.rawclobber$//eventList[@name=\"PLANET_ENGE_BUNKER\"]/event[3]/choice[4]/text"
msgstr "Leave the bunker."

#: src-ru/data/events.xml.rawclobber:12118
msgid ""
"data/events.xml.rawclobber$//eventList[@name=\"PLANET_ENGE_BUNKER\"]/event[3]/choice[4]/event/text"
msgstr ""
"Here everything looks like it was about to collapse, there was still not "
"enough to arrange explosions.You decide not to risk the team and give the "
"order to return to the ship.Soon the engines are heated, and you are ready "
"to make another jump."

#: src-ru/data/events.xml.rawclobber:12125
msgid ""
"data/events.xml.rawclobber$//eventList[@name=\"PLANET_ENGE_ONE_MISSLE\"]/event[1]/text"
msgstr ""
"You lay a missile projectile under one of the doors.An explosion is heard, "
"and a bunch of dust rises into the air.When she dissipates, you see that the"
" steel door did not even bent!You do not risk laying another shell, who "
"knows how many more these walls will withstand before falling.The team "
"returns to the ship, and you give the order to jump."

#: src-ru/data/events.xml.rawclobber:12128
msgid ""
"data/events.xml.rawclobber$//eventList[@name=\"PLANET_ENGE_ONE_MISSLE\"]/event[2]/text"
msgstr ""
"You lay a missile projectile under one of the doors.An explosion is heard, "
"and a bunch of dust rises into the air.When it dissipates, you see that the "
"steel door was knocked out by an explosion, it is lying near the entrance to"
" the spacious room.Your crew goes inside.Most of all, it looks like a "
"laboratory or some assembly workshop.Unknown mechanisms are everywhere, "
"everything is covered with a large layer of dust and most likely does not "
"work.Your attention is attracted by one device that is still in working "
"condition.The instructions say that it allows you to improve any missile gun"
" installed on the ship, so that it will not need ammunition!It looks very "
"attractive."

#: src-ru/data/events.xml.rawclobber:12137
msgid ""
"data/events.xml.rawclobber$//textList[@name=\"PLANET_ENGE_UPGRADE_TEXT\"]/text"
msgstr ""
"You set your tool in the mechanism.He begins to carry out the necessary "
"adjustments ..."

#: src-ru/data/events.xml.rawclobber:12140
msgid ""
"data/events.xml.rawclobber$//textList[@name=\"PLANET_ENGE_UPGRADE_TEXT_2\"]/text"
msgstr ""
"... and finally improves your gun.Now ammunition will not end when shooting "
"from it!You are still a step closer to the fulfillment of your mission, and "
"now it's time to prepare for a jump."

